1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.045
Welcome to Dynamics Data Export!

2
00:00:03.045 --> 00:00:06.707
In this video series, you'll learn about a powerful reporting feature 

3
00:00:06.707 --> 00:00:08.591
in Knox Asset Intelligence 

4
00:00:08.592 --> 00:00:13.266
that lets you create customized reports tailored to your business needs.

5
00:00:13.666 --> 00:00:20.034
Dynamics Data Export, or DDE for short, lets you build customized reports by combining

6
00:00:20.035 --> 00:00:23.499
multiple data insights like low battery events,

7
00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:25.266
mobile network usage,

8
00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:27.400
and app abnormal events

9
00:00:27.833 --> 00:00:29.566
into a single report.

10
00:00:30.133 --> 00:00:33.566
This means you can get a complete picture of your device fleet

11
00:00:33.566 --> 00:00:37.066
without the hassle of cross-referencing multiple sources.

12
00:00:37.066 --> 00:00:41.266
We'll walk you through selecting measures and dimensions,

13
00:00:41.266 --> 00:00:47.199
applying filters and choosing visualization formats, such as a table for detailed analysis,

14
00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:49.800
a line graph to spot trends over time,

15
00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:53.466
or a pie chart to show proportions at a glance.

16
00:00:53.966 --> 00:00:56.897
Whether you're investigating battery drain issues, 

17
00:00:56.898 --> 00:00:58.711
tracking app usage patterns, 

18
00:00:58.711 --> 00:01:00.802
or preparing a report for leadership,

19
00:01:00.803 --> 00:01:05.675
Dynamic Data Export gives you the tools to share fleet insights with technical teams

20
00:01:05.675 --> 00:01:07.586
and business stakeholders alike.

21
00:01:07.587 --> 00:01:11.166
Letting you tell your data story clearly and effectively.

22
00:01:11.633 --> 00:01:12.799
Ready to dive in?

23
00:01:13.233 --> 00:01:16.652
in the next video, we'll cover measures and dimensions, 

24
00:01:16.652 --> 00:01:19.066
the building blocks of every great report.

25
00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:21.233
Let's get started!

